{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/225-ideas-for-a-mummy-chronicle","id":225,"title":"Ideas for a Mummy Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T09:50:57-07:00","id":225,"title":"Ideas for a Mummy Chronicle","content":"Just wanted to say first of all how much I'm enjoying the Mummy: the Curse book now I have my grubby mitts on it. Delays can be frustrating, but I can say that in this instance it was totally worth it!<br /> <br /> Now I'm looking at how to put a game together for my (very enthusiastic) group, and I'm hitting a bit of a stumbling block. Just like with Promethean, I love the game but I'm struggling to come up with a good group dynamic. How can I get my group together and staying together, without stretching the boundaries of the setting? I know there are some ideas in the GM's guide, but my group will all want to be mummies, and I don't want to limit character generation too much.<br /> <br /> Love to hear some pitches for a starting idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/33-nifara","name":"Nifara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar33_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T13:22:18-07:00","id":424,"title":"","content":"I haven't read it yet myself, but Guildhalls of the Deathless gives spells for connecting Arisen to each other, so that when one wakes up they all do. That could be one place to look. <br /> <br /> Another idea is to have them all share the same cult, just different aspects of it. Meaning the cult is super powerful, but some of the Mummies have more spiritual control over it than the others. That way players spending more Merit dots get their points back, and you have a convenient reason why they all wake up at the same time.<br /> <br /> If the game takes place during a Sothic turn you could tell the players they all have vague memories of each other, giving the Mummies an incentive to stay near the other Mummies. Or you could say the other in the meret Arisen are the only things they remember clearly, making the group all work as an anchor for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But that would be *shudders* <i>fun</i>!<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/119-strapping-gent","name":"Strapping Gent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T16:20:09-07:00","id":648,"title":"","content":"Our group is planning to have one or two mummies and the rest of the party will be their cultists. Gentleman Gamer ran a pretty cool game with CAS and Mark Rein*Hagen that used that party composition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T02:53:52-07:00","id":1010,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd be annoyed to buy into playing a game about Mummies and play...a non-Mummy. Same reason I don't get on with Ars Magica troupe play. I signed up to play a Wizard, not a wizard's house cleaner.<br /> <br /> For Mummy I'd recommend trying the PCs be part of newly founding cult. Their Tombs or Bodies are found by some inquisitive locals or revealed by an earthquake or something and the small local group gathers them up triggering the PCs first awakening in a long, long time. Their old cults lost to the winds, their old ties and connections vanishingly small (only their Guild Memberships remain imprinted on their five-fold souls).<br /> <br /> Then your players can start confused with some vague purpose related to building their cult from these newly inquisitive locals. The locals don't really know what they are and the PCs don't really know much else either. I recommend setting it somewhere like Indonesia, a bit out of the way, enough smaller villages dotted around but growing interconnectivity, burgeoning wealth, etc.<br /> <br /> This way you've got a clean slate for the PCs to get comfortable with but you know you;re missing 6 thousand years of history and you're in a position where someone or something must have destroyed your old cults and cast you into the earth never to be found again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T10:50:40-07:00","id":1162,"title":"","content":"Im currently running a table-top chronicle set in Washington, DC. My players get to play 2 characters: a cultist (some who are psychics) and an Arisen. At any one time there are 1-2 Arisen active, the other players play their cult followers. Everyone gets to play their Mummy and none of my players feel annoyed at this set up (and yes, Ars Magica troupe style works ideally for this campaign). For anyone interested my players have been posted recaps, feel free to peruse/mine for ideas.<br /> <br /> The campaign page is here: <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/messages/boards/thread/33478092\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-So...hread/33478092</a><br /> <br /> The recaps are posted here: <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/messages/boards/thread/34979562\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-So...hread/34979562</a><br /> <br /> The campaing culminates with the Sothic Turn in 2012, and chronicles the stories of these Arisen on the eve of this major event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":311,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","user":"JoeB","date":". 11-02-2013, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T06:43:56-08:00","id":1708,"title":"","content":"I'm getting ready to run the intro adventure for my group, and basically our work around is that they all pooled their Cult and Tomb merits. The basic premise of our chronicle is going to be that they were assigned together as a group back in the nameless empire for some purpose (that they don't remember) and that until that purpose if fulfilled (if ever, if it's even possible) they're tied together. Raising one raises them all, and they're kind of stuck with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}